{
 "product": "Kimi Code (MoonshotAI/kimi-code, v2.6.3, the real `kimi -p` headless loop)",
 "component": "The real Kimi Code v2.6.3 `kimi -p` headless loop (the shipped non-interactive print mode, `--output-format stream-json`) running the real Kimi Code agent loop (the SDK KimiHarness agent over the `openai` provider protocol) against the Trustrun tool set (search_docs, calculator, plus the monitor/grader/clarification tools run_audit adds) as real MCP tools executed in-process behind an HTTP bridge. The stub's tool decisions are rendered as direct `mcp__trustrun__<name>` tool calls; the MCP server executes each call through the bridge and Kimi Code feeds the bare tool text back as the next tool message. The driver runs under the project venv python and drives the published npm package's dist/main.mjs via node as one subprocess per call. No key, no network. The loop ends on a text response, so multi-hop tasks can complete. Tool results reach the model verbatim as bare-text tool messages.",
